==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|fliohan|lang=goh}}, from {{proto|gem-pro|fleuhanan|lang=de}}. Cognate with Dutch {{term|vlieden}} and English {{term|flee}}.

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=2|flieht|floh|geflohen|auxiliary=both}}

# {{intransitive|auxiliary: “[[sein]]”}} to [[flee]]; to [[escape]]
# {{intransitive|auxiliary: “[[sein]]”}} to [[diverge]]
#: ''Die Linien '''fliehen'''.'' — “The lines diverge.”
# {{transitive|auxiliary: “[[haben]]”}} to [[flee]] from (someone); to [[avoid]]

